{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1200471-micro-template-awakened-engineers-or-yet-another-genius-take","id":1200471,"title":"Micro-Template: Awakened Engineers (or, yet another Genius take)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-28T10:24:20-07:00","id":1200471,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Micro-Template: Awakened Engineers (or, yet another Genius take)","content":"<b>Preface</b><br /> I was digging around in the Homebrew Mage Merits thread and was brainstorming a way for Sleepwalkers to use the Enhanced Item and Imbued Item Merits easier. Sure, they just <i>can</i> have said items, and acquire new ones by just &quot;buying&quot; more instances of those Merits, but what if you want them to have those options in Mage absent and restricted settings? I made a person-focused Enhanced Item Merit (of questionable quality), where they can switch around the bonuses. Imbued Item, with activated spells, Mana costs, and dice pools, is harder.<br /> <br /> But what is someone who can make Imbued Items, but not perform the actual magic they hold? Basically a Gadgeteer, or (one concept of) a Genius. Now, there are more mechanics than just &quot;you can make Imbued Items&quot;, and allowing anyone to just make whatever spell effects they want (and can pay for) is excessive, putting it into a micro-template structure gives more options while slowing down the power growth. <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Phase 1: Brainstorming</span></b><br /> <br /> So, let's call the baseline Merit <b>Insight</b> at the moment. Each dot of Insight will allow for a Mana Pool, at least, for the powering of various Mana-dependent items. If we are representing devices and Enhanced and Imbued Items (as per the Merits), this is going to get XP costly, fast. So what about allowing them to have Obsessions as well? In theme, and allowing the Arcane Beats (and XP) to be spent on Enhanced and Imbued Item Merits off-sets the big costs. Insight also needs to grant access to &quot;spells&quot; (Arcana + Practice) to be able to incorporate into Enhanced and Imbued items they &quot;make&quot;. Either it can be tied directly to Insight, or Insight can grant free instances of tag on Merits that can be purchased separately to expand their repertoire.<br /> <br /> <u>Follow-up questions:</u><br /> <b>Mage-Sight </b>- Core ability (in limited form) or purchasable Merit?<br /> <b>Attainments </b>- Granted by Insight, unlock via virtual Arcana, or make it a spell effect of the equivalent Arcana rating?<br /> <b>Mana acquisition </b>- Allow Pattern Scouring, Hallow Oblation, Legacy-like Oblation? Part of Insight, locked behind a Merit, or restricted entirely?<br /> <b>Power acqusition </b>- Let them buy Arcana outright (though only usable for determining Enhanced/Imbued Item effects), or use a Arcana + Practice combo?<br /> <b>Other Abilities</b> - Beyond building Enhanced and Imbued Items (however useful and flexible those are), what other powers and perks should they get?<br /> <b>Drawbacks</b> - With Great Power, Comes Great Insanity. Or, how should being this micro-template suck worse than being a &quot;normal&quot; Sleepwalker? <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Phase 2: Mechanics</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23896\" data-vbnamecard=\"23896\">Mirthless</a> has created an excellent version <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1200471-micro-template-awakened-engineers-or-yet-another-genius-take?p=1217297#post1217297\">here</a>. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Phase 3: Examples</b></span><br /> <br /> [Pending]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-11-2018, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T14:50:05-07:00","id":1200592,"title":"","content":"Basing them off Proximi sounds workable. Each Blessing is a <i>Working</i> they can manifest as magical items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T14:57:09-07:00","id":1200595,"title":"","c