,"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T15:51:02-07:00","id":1200616,"title":"","content":"That sounds more like an alternate mage than a supporting splat, but oh well. <br /> <br /> How\u2019d they interact with the Crafting rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T16:07:07-07:00","id":1200623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1200471-micro-template-awakened-engineers-or-yet-another-genius-take?p=1200616#post1200616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds more like an alternate mage than a supporting splat, but oh well. </div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they aren't a full Mage in the slightest - basically just the minimum necessary to create and sustain Enhanced and Imbued items. They can't use the Arcana for actual casting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1200471-micro-template-awakened-engineers-or-yet-another-genius-take?p=1200616#post1200616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How\u2019d they interact with the Crafting rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally? Unless you have other ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T16:13:25-07:00","id":1200624,"title":"","content":"Oh, it wasn\u2019t that I had further ideas - just shooting in the dark here. It\u2019s just that my line of thought for homebrew nowadays has \u201canything already printed that I can use\u201d as default. <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, Hallows and Tass feels like the default, if not the only, way these guys get Mana for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T17:00:43-07:00","id":1200641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1200471-micro-template-awakened-engineers-or-yet-another-genius-take?p=1200624#post1200624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, it wasn\u2019t that I had further ideas - just shooting in the dark here. It\u2019s just that my line of thought for homebrew nowadays has \u201canything already printed that I can use\u201d as default. <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, Hallows and Tass feels like the default, if not the only, way these guys get Mana for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Building Equipment rules can be used for the Enhancing/Imbuing operation? I have to review that.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Hallows/Tass is probably where they get most of it. Maybe a more general Oblation? But limited in repeat time (like Alchemists, Magnitude, and Pyros).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T04:08:55-07:00","id":1200753,"title":"","content":"So, some basic thoughts that may or may not be useful:<br /> <br /> First, you mentioned the experience cost, which does seem like kind of a problem. Perhaps you could build something along the lines of any of the following:<ul><li>A \u2018multiplier\u2019 effect that lets the Gadgeteer create more points\u2019 worth of gadgets for the same resource investment.</li> <li>A multiplier effect along a different axis: Let the Gadgeteer create certain basic Imbued/Enhanced items in multiple groups: These could then be traded or given to other group members to help expand abilities.</li> <li>A number of \u2018free\u2019 dots in Imbued or Enhanced items that cost no merits and may be switched out fairly easily (thus hopefully making the users slightly more versatile).</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Mostly, I figure that one of the balancing factors for Imbued Items is that mages are very versatile and an imbued item is basically useful to them as both a mana battery and a way to expand into abilities they do not possess. Gadgeteers don\u2019t have a use for Mana, and don\u2019t have any inherent powers to expand their abilities away from, so might need a bit of a boost to have their Imbued Items be an interesting choice for them.<br /> <br /> With that particular bit of unsolicited opinion out of the way (:P):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mage-Sight </b>- Core ability (in limited form) or purchasable Merit? </div> </div> </div>Between your choice, a purchaseable Merit but preferably one that manifests as an item. Gadgeteers are crafters, so let them get it as a particular form of magic item. Probably by treating it the same way you end up treating Attainments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Attainments </b>- Granted by Insight, unlock via virtual Arcana, or make it a spell effect of the equivalent Arcana rating? </div> </div> </div>Would you like them to have Attainments as a power for themselves, or for use within Gadgets? For the former I\u2019d go with the equivalent Arcana rating. For the latter I\u2019d go with granting them through virtual Arcana, subject to the same limits as Imbued Items already have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mana acquisition </b>- Allow Pattern Scouring, Hallow Oblation, Legacy-like Oblation? Part of Insight, locked behind a Merit, or restricted entirely? </div> </div> </div>Mana production through scouring seems like a good idea, given that it\u2019s inherently a limited act. As a bonus, you could probably spin it into a merit of its own and that Merit would be a useful thing for a Sleepwalker to have even without them being Gadgeteers. Or at least, it would be a useful thing for a Mage with access to that Sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Power acqusition </b>- Let them buy Arcana outright (though only usable for determining Enhanced/Imbued Item effects), or use a Arcana + Practice combo? </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d go with outright Arcana buying, given that their powers already cost experience to obtain, so I wouldn\u2019t make it any more difficult than it is already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Other Abilities</b> - Beyond building Enhanced and Imbued Items (however useful and flexible those are), what other powers and perks should they get? </div> </div> </div>A general bonus to Crafting rolls might be a nice touch. Perhaps take some inspiration from the vehicle modding merit that\u2019s...somewhere. Maybe even let it work best on anything that\u2019s already an Imbued or Enhanced Item. That way, your gadgeteers aren\u2019t limited to modern science or sheer occultism but can combine both.<br /> <br /> Perhaps add in a way for Gadgeteers to come together more in a particular way. One of the reasons Mage has a society to begin with is because they have stuff like Rotes sitting right at the top of their Attainment pyramid. Perhaps an equivalent ability for Gadgeteers (Schematics? I\u2019m kind of drawing on <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Urxj0z6zvILm6-RAdUWXi5X_M6ppIjQ54H2Cb_prQM/edit#heading=h.24vbknn3cza4\" target=\"_blank\">Pendragon\u2019s Sons of Bezalel</a> here) would give them good reason to congregate <i>and</i> allow a bit more differentiation between Gadgeteers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Drawbacks</b> - With Great Power, Comes Great Insanity. Or, how should being this micro-template suck worse than being a &quot;normal&quot; Sleepwalker? </div> </div> </div>From a storytelling perspective, these people would be <i>valuable</i>, even more so than regular Sleepwalkers. So one thing that immediately comes to mind is \u201cthey routinely come to the attention of Mages, which is a pretty bad thing for anyone who is not a Mage themselves\u201d. Regularly attracting powerful people who would probably <i>love</i> for you to work for them to make stuff is probably not very good for your health and sanity.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t really think of a particular inherent disadvantage, other than that we are essentially talking about people who draw upon the Supernal without having written their name on a Watchtower. Archmages can do that because they\u2019re powerful enough to create a safe space for themselves in the Supernal. Proximi do it because of spells cast by very powerful supernal beings.<br /> <br /> These guys? They don\u2019t. A Mage that goes into the Supernal erases themselves from history. Maybe Gadgeteers should have a similar issue where they\u2019ve got more and more trouble interacting with \u2018normal\u2019 people as their arts effectively put them at one remove from the world? I dunno. It doesn\u2019t feel quite right to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T06:47:45-07:00","id":1200787,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23896\" data-vbnamecard=\"23896\">Mirthless</a>.<br /> <br /> So, as far as naming goes, I'm thinking <b>Artificers</b> would be appropriate, due to the connotations of Items, Art, and vaguely Magic.<br /> <br /> It looks like Insight is going to have to: Grant a Mana Pool, allow for some slow Mana generation to compensate for those that lack access to Hallows, and offer some &quot;freebie&quot; Enchanced/Imbued Item points to limit the pain of the XP costs. It inherently grants the ability to Enhance and Imbue despite lacking Gnosis and Arcana (traditionally), bypass the Attainment limits for Imbued Items, and allow Enhanced and Imbued Items to be &quot;recycled&quot; to free up the points/XP for new creations. And maybe recharge Imbued Items without Channel Mana?<br /> <br /> Mage Sight should either be handled as a 1-dot Spell Effect or just use Knowing or Unveiling. Either way, it should be incorporated into an item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T10:04:28-07:00","id":1200849,"title":"","content":"I feel like the ability to create Imbued and Enhanced items is far too powerful for a micro-template.<br /> <br /> As a one-off Mystery (this Sleepwalker has the ability to craft such items!) it would be really cool, but otherwise they're just Mages that can't cast.<br /> <br /> If you want to make the Awakened more heavily reliant on Imbued and Enhanced items you could remove Instant casting as an option and give everyone the ability to Imbue, even without Prime 4. Maybe those with Prime 4 can relinquish their items, but those without can't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T10:28:02-07:00","id":1200860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1200471-micro-template-awakened-engineers-or-yet-another-genius-take?p=1200849#post1200849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the ability to create Imbued and Enhanced items is far too powerful for a micro-template.<br /> <br /> As a one-off Mystery (this Sleepwalker has the ability to craft such items!) it would be really cool, but otherwise they're just Mages that can't cast.<br /> <br /> If you want to make the Awakened more heavily reliant on Imbued and Enhanced items you could remove Instant casting as an option and give everyone the ability to Imbue, even without Prime 4. Maybe those with Prime 4 can relinquish their items, but those without can't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as we've seen, Imbued and Enhanced Items are very expensive, XP-wise. Considering the typically low Mana-pools for Imbued Items, Artificers won't be busting out their tricks very often. They are actually lower powered than Proximi, since Blessings don't <i>always</i> need Mana (I'm pretty sure).<br /> <br /> This is more for the <i>feel</i> of playing with characters whose powers derive from their tools, and explore to expand their knowledge and options. It isn't meant as a Mage replacement. (Besides Imbued Items aren't necessarily faster - Reach still needs to be spent on Ritual-&gt;Instant casting)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-29-2018, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T11:17:23-07:00","id":1200890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1200471-micro-template-awakened-engineers-or-yet-another-genius-take?p=1200860#post1200860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, as we've seen, Imbued and Enhanced Items are very expensive, XP-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creating, and safely relinquishing, an Imbued or Enhanced item costs between 0 and 1 XP per spell, assuming you always buy back lost Willpower dots. Unsafely relinquishing is always free, and if it's an Enhancement that lasts for only a week or so it's not even dangerous to do so. Purchasing the item with merit dots represents you getting it from someone else, not you making it.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, for a Sleepwalker artificer I'd do something like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Imbument (*** - *****)</b><br /> <br /> When a character takes this merit they choose one Arcana. That Arcana defines the types of items that can be crafted and shapes the character's life, should they ever fully Awaken they will inevitably Awaken to the path for which their chosen Arcana is a ruling Arcana.<br /> The character gains a mana pool equal to the number of dots they have in this merit, can only spend 1 mana/turn, and gains the ability to transfer mana to any Imbued item they created. They also gain the ability to scour their pattern for mana once per day (p. 87 of M:tAw 2e).<br /> At three dots in this merit, the character can learn to Imbue items with one dot spells of the appropriate Arcana, four dots in the merit grants access to two dot spells, and five dots to three.<br /> The character automatically knows a number of spells equal to their dots in this merit, and can purchase additional spells for 1 XP per spell.<br /> When Imbuing the character rolls their dots in this merit as their dicepool and otherwise obeys all the rules for Imbuing items (p. 195-6 M:tAw 2e).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T13:41:19-07:00","id":1202301,"title":"","content":"Here's a rough concept - on available Arcana - thoughts?<br /> <br /> For each dot of Insight, the Artificer has access to one Arcana (as if they had 1 dot in that Arcana, so Knowing, Unveiling, and Compelling). They can pick up a Merit (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) that grants access to Arcana 2 and 3, respectively in the Arcana they have access to (with an even more optional Advanced version for Arcana 4 and 5). This gives access for up to 5 Arcana, at ratings of up to 3 (or 5).<br /> <br /> OR have each dot of Insight grant a &quot;free&quot; dot in an Arcana. That would allow specialization into one field, or branching out. Make additional dots purchasable.<br /> <br /> Actually making items is handled via the Imbued Item rules, and the Artificer pays the XP for the permanent item. They can break down items they've made for the &quot;resources&quot; (IE, Sanctity of Merits).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-02-2018, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T04:31:40-07:00","id":1202524,"title":"","content":"I favor your first option, especially with regards to scalability and the fact that this makes it an inherently customizable option whether or not to allow Artificers to make 4/5 dot spells.<br /> <br /> I also like the choice for making Imbued Items more or less as normal, because that also allows for a few 'free' items by not releasing it from spell control. By default, a Sleepwalker can already hold spells in Spell Control (1 or 2, depending on the caster's connection). More if they have the Banner-Bearer merit, which I think means that dovetails nicely.<br /> <br /> One question that remains regarding imbuement: Normally, the roll is Gnosis+Prime. However, the Artificers as written do not have either Gnosis or 'true' Prime, so they'd need a substitute for them. Insight + Craft, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:46:26-07:00","id":1202578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mirthless</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1200471-micro-template-awakened-engineers-or-yet-another-genius-take?p=1202524#post1202524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I favor your first option, especially with regards to scalability and the fact that this makes it an inherently customizable option whether or not to allow Artificers to make 4/5 dot spells.<br /> <br /> I also like the choice for making Imbued Items more or less as normal, because that also allows for a few 'free' items by not releasing it from spell control. By default, a Sleepwalker can already hold spells in Spell Control (1 or 2, depending on the caster's connection). More if they have the Banner-Bearer merit, which I think means that dovetails nicely.<br /> <br /> One question that remains regarding imbuement: Normally, the roll is Gnosis+Prime. However, the Artificers as written do not have either Gnosis or 'true' Prime, so they'd need a substitute for them. Insight + Craft, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds about right. As far as Spell Control, Artificers would still need some, as they lack Gnosis. Maybe 1, or scaled to Insight? Or 1, with optional Merits providing more (like I wrote for Proximi). Retained Spell control lets them adjust the effects of Imbued Items at will (and cancel their effects outright).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T01:55:12-07:00","id":1217297,"title":"","content":"Hey all,<br /> <br /> So I spent some time building this stuff to put some of the discussion from this thread into practice. I'm posting this here with Vent0's permission (as well as considerable help in proofreading and brainstorming), in the hope that others can get some use out of it or use it as inspiration for further work. Much thanks to Vent0 for his help.<br /> <br /> <b>What is an Artificer?</b><br /> <br /> A subset of Sleepwalkers who are capable of creating Imbued Items and often have additional abilities related to crafting.<br /> <br /> <b>Creating an Artificer</b><br /> <br /> To create an Artificer, use all the rules for creating a starting Chronicles of Darkness character. Additionally, Artificers start the game with the Sleepwalker, Artificer and Schema User merits and one dot each in the Create Item and Item Resonance merits.<br /> <br /> <i>Sidebar: Learning Artifice</i><br /> <br /> Artificers normally start off as Sleepwalkers and slowly gain proficiency in Imbuement under a teacher, who can be either a fellow Sleepwalker or a Mage with similar abilities. Those mentors normally have Schemata of their own, as well as a store of various items.<br /> <br /> In those cases, the first ability to be learned is usually Schema User, allowing for the reproduction of existing items. From there, they learn Item Resonance to both improve their facility with crafting and get more use out of using the Items themselves. From there, Artificer first allows for the recharging of items from a Hallow, and when combined with Imbue Item then allows for creating Items of one\u2019s own.<br /> <br /> In general, the mentoring process (or continuing education when creating a \u2018base\u2019 artificer) can be modeled using the Mentor Merit, while later students can be modeled using the Retainer Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Artificers, Spell Control and Relinquishment</b><br /> <br /> Artificers are not Mages and, as such, do not normally have Spell Control for themselves. However, Artificers <i>are</i> Sleepwalkers and as such have some limited ability to hold spells within their souls as listed under \u201cShield Maidens and Flag Bearers\u201d (Mage, p.303-304). An Artificer has a Connected sympathy to themselves and, as such, has up to three Imbued spells held within their souls, which can be increased as normal through the Banner-Bearer merit. Additionally, many experienced Artificers have apprentices and assistants who are likewise Sleepwalkers and capable of holding spells for the Artificers if they agree.<br /> <br /> Unlike Mages, however, Artificers <i>must</i> be able to create an item within their existing Control level. They do not get the option of increasing Reach effects as Mages do: If they have used all three available slots, they must first destroy or relinquish one of their existing items before making a new one.<br /> <br /> Additionally, Artificers lack the supernal knowledge to relinquish a spell in any but the most costly ways. When they use a Willpower point to relinquish a spell, add the Item\u2019s highest Arcanum rating to the amount of Reach over the limit they have gone when determining the Paradox pool. Using a Willpower dot allows for safe relinquishment.<br /> <br /> <b>Artificers and Paths</b><br /> <br /> Sleepwalker Artificers, not being Mages, do not have a Path and cannot, by default, create any magical items reliant on having a Path, such as those using the Apocalypse spell. In some cases, such as with Proximi, Artificers <i>do</i> have a Path and follow its rules instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits for Artificers</b><br /> <br /> The following Merits are intended for (though not strictly limited to) Artificers and include the base Artificer ability.<br /> <br /> In addition, certain other Merits available to Sleepwalkers are particularly appropriate. These include Banner Bearer (Mage 2e, p. 305), Relic Attuned (Mage 2e, p.306) and Cup Holder (found <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1x7u00BCYHSh-WSGe2krR0hYiienVZ0VidH4DAKPNXTc/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>).<br /> <br /> <b>Artificer (<span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Sleepwalker or Awakened<br /> <i>Effect: </i>Your character has access to the Imbue Item Attainment despite lacking the requisite ability in the Prime Arcanum and gains the ability to Imbue any spell they are capable of casting. Furthermore, they may substitute their rating in the Arcanum used for Prime when rolling to create the Item. If your character ever achieves 4 dots in Prime, they may choose to lose this Merit under the Sanctity of Merits.<br /> <br /> Additionally, your character may charge Imbued Items and Artifacts with Mana from any source available to them. This Merit explicitly allows the use of Oblations at a Hallow, provided that the resulting Mana is immediately used to charge an Imbued Item or Artifact. Your character may use a similar process to expend Mana in order to create Imbued Items in the first place.<br /> <br /> <b>Item Sensitivity (<span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisites: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Awakened or Artificer</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Your character gains the ability to sense magical items, be they Enhanced, Imbued, Artifacts or any other type of object imbued with magical power. For Mages, this manifests as an additional trigger to their Peripheral Mage Sight. For Artificers, it counts as the Unseen Sense merit attuned to Imbued Items, Enhanced Items and Artifacts. Taking the Spooked Condition additionally gives a hint as to how this item works.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Create Item (<span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2022,\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Artificer or Awakened<br /> <i>Effect: </i>Choose an Arcanum. When creating Imbued Items, your character has effective dots in this Arcanum equal to half their dots in this merit, rounded up. This allows them to create Imbued Items (including the applicable Attainments) of this Arcanum.<br /> <br /> If the character possesses any dots in the relevant Arcanum, refund a commensurate amount of experiences for this Merit (1 for one dot, 3 for two dots, and all 5 for 3 dots).<br /> <br /> <b>Specialist Crafter (<span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2022 or \u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: </i>At least one effective dot in the chosen spell\u2019s Arcanum<br /> <i>Effect: </i>Your character has a specialized ability to Imbue certain spells into Items. <br /> <br /> At two dots, choose a single spell no more than one dot higher than the character\u2019s effective Arcanum rating. She has the ability to Imbue that specific spell as though all her Arcana were one dot higher. At four dots, she may instead choose a spell up to two dots higher as though her Arcana were two dots higher. <br /> <br /> This Merit does not allow for the creation of Imbued Items that use the Imperial Practices, nor allow for any Arcanum\u2019s effective dots to be above 5. If your character increases her Arcana ratings such that she can Imbue the spell on her own, she may choose to lose the merit and be refunded the experiences.<br /> <br /> <b>Item Resonance (<span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Artificer or Awakened<br /> <i>Effect: </i>Your character\u2019s soul has far more facility with Imbued Items than most of her kind. <br /> <br /> When creating or using an Imbued item, increase her effective Gnosis by the dots in this merit. This may not push a Mage above 10 effective dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Empower Item (<span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisites: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Ability to Imbue Item</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">When crafting an Item, your character may assign additional successes to increase the effective Gnosis of any user of the item, up to a maximum of their own Gnosis dots when creating Items. This may not push the user\u2019s effective Gnosis beyond 5 dots.</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Note: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">When taking the Imbued Item Merit, this activation bonus should be bought the same manner as extra Mana: Each effective Gnosis increase is worth an additional Merit dot.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Pattern Sacrifice (<span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisites: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Sleepwalker</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Your characters gains the ability to Scour your Pattern for Mana in the same way a Gnosis 1 Mage could. He may then immediately channel this Mana to an available container, or spend it in place of Willpower to activate any supernatural ability you possess. If your character does not immediately start spending Mana, it is lost unless he has a merit such as Cup Holder that allows you to retain it.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Schema User (<span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Your character may use <i>Schemata</i>: A set of instructions to build an Imbued Item that can makes use of a particular spell, even when you lack the ability to ordinarily craft Imbued Items. This requires all the normal rolls to create Imbued Items, though your character may do so as though he possessed five dots in both Prime and the relevant Arcanum. Attainments may not be incorporated into the spell.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">As a special rule, Artifacts <i>always</i> count as Schemata for the spells that they can cast. They are thus particularly prized by those Artificers who hold them.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Schema (\u2022+)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisite: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Schema User</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">You possess a Schema and can use it to reproduce items. The cost of a Schema is equal to the number of unique Arcana used, plus one for each Arcanum over three dots.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Reproduce Schema </span>(<span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisites: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Schema User, ability to Imbue Items.</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect:</span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> You may reproduce a Schema as though it were an Imbued Item, using the same rules as though you were creating a Schema of your own. Doing so requires you to have at least one (effective) dot in all Arcana that exist within the Schema, as well as access to the Schema itself.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Craft Schema </span>(<span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisites: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Reproduce Schema, five effective Arcanum dots in the use of at least one spell, effective Gnosis of 3+ when creating Imbued Items.</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect:</span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> At the pinnacle of crafting ability, you gain the ability to create new Schemata. This requires an effective Arcanum rating of five dots in the spell used to create the Schemata and is done in the same way as creating an Imbued Item, with the following changes:</span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Schemata never hold Mana.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The roll time is eight hours.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Schemata can never be released for a point of Willpower.</span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Item Enhancer (\u2022+)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisites: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Artificer orAwakened</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect:</span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Your character gains a floating set of points that can be used to create Enhanced Items equal to their dots in this Merit. These provide a bonus to a tool, a point of Structure, or a point of Durability to any physical object.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Your may reassign points by spending one hour and paying a point of Mana or Willpower (as desired) for each point so reassigned. Unlike ordinary Enhanced Items, your character must pay a point of Mana or Willpower to activate the bonus for the scene (which only works for you). If the Item carrying the tool bonus is destroyed, the bonus returns to your character for assignment later. Finally, a character who loses access to an Enhanced Item can disenchant it remotely, losing the dots (and regaining them through Sanctity of Merits, the dots cannot be returned to Item Enhancer until the start of the next story).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">This Merit can go over five dots, though no tool may gain more than five supernatural bonus dice through any combination of supernatural powers that include this merit.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Arcanum Enhancement (\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisites: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Item Enhancer, ability to Imbue Items</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Choose an Arcanum. You gain the ability to assign your floating dots from Item Enhancer to persistent spell effects from that Arcanum as per the Enhanced Item merit. Doing so requires the ability to Imbue that spell into an item.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Technomagic (\u2022\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisites: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Item Enhancer</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Your character is especially skilled at enhancing items she has built herself. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">At two dots, your character no longer needs to spend Mana or Willpower to activate the bonus to Enhanced Items she has created herself.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">At four dots, when assigning floating bonus dice from Item Enhancer, if your character assigns the dice to an object they created themselves, waive an amount of the dot cost equal to half her dice pool when creating it (rounded down), to a minimum of one dot. She still need sufficient total floating dots to enhance the item in the first place.</span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Example: Alice wants to make an enhanced computer: She rolls Computer + Intelligence to build the computer (or any other viable Crafting dice pool: Let's pretend this is the right one). She's got Computer 3, Intelligence 4, and 4 dots in Item Enhancer. She currently possesses no items that have been enhanced.<br /> <br /> Her dice pool is 7 dice, which translates to a discount of 3 dots. Thus, she can give a +4 bonus to her crafted item, but only use one of her floating dots in Item Enhancer. If she only had 3 dots in Item Enhancer, she could only give a +3 bonus.<br /> <br /> Let's say Alice does make her computer and imbues it with a +4 bonus. She now has 3 floating dots of Enhanced Item left. If she wanted to do the same thing to another computer, she could only enhance it by up to 3 points, as that is the maximum she could now Imbue.</span></i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Imbue Attainment (\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisites: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Ability to Imbue Items</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Choose an Arcanum for which your character can craft Imbued Items (including through the Create Item merit). For this Arcanum, she can then create Attainment Items, treating each Attainment as though it were a spell (including the potential to Imbue higher-level Attainments through Specialist Crafter). Additionally, for the purpose of this Merit, Mage Sight is considered an Attainment available at one dot.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Attainment Items function and are made - and costed, if bought - as Imbued Items, with the following exceptions and clarifications:</span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Attainments can be imbued into items at varying Arcana ratings (and count as a spell of that rating). This then determines the Merit dot cost of the Item, its difficulty in crafting, and its effects when used. An Attainment\u2019s minimum rating is always equal to its prerequisite Arcanum rating, and its maximum rating is equal to your own rating in an Arcanum (including any Applicable bonuses from </span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Attainment Items do not normally activate: Instead, they grant their ability to anyone carrying them, though the first time in any scene they benefit from the power drains a point of Mana from the item in addition to any other costs - and the item fails to activate if it is empty.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The Attainment Item\u2019s Mana may be used to pay for any costs used in the Attainment.</span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Further, some specific rules exist for particular Attainments:</span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The effects of Mage Sight differ by path. Possession of this Item does not grant Peripheral Mage Sight.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Eyes of the Death, Mind\u2019s Eye and Spirit Eyes work as normal for those with Mage Sight. Those who do not possess Mage Sight instead act as though having Peripheral Mage Sight (for purposes of this item only), and can gain the equivalent of Active Mage Sight (for purpose of this item only) by spending a further point of Mana.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Improved Pattern Restoration functions as normal (for physical restoration only) for non-Mages despite Pattern Restoration ordinarily being unavailable. The Item\u2019s Mana may explicitly be spent for Pattern Restoration.</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Targeted Summoning only summons Supernal Entities from your Path. If you imbue one of your Ruling Arcana, this instead grants the ability to summon an entity at all. </span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">The Imbue Item and Create Rote Attainments cannot be made into Attainment Items.</span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Path Mimicry (\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Prerequisites: </span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Ability to Imbue Items</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Effect:</span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Choose a Path that you do not have. Your character gains the ability to briefly mimic this Path. This requires contact with a strong sympathetic link to said Path - such as a Mage, Proximus, or an appropriate Artifact, Aedes or Verge. By spending a willpower point, your character can then forge an artificial connection to the Path, allowing him to Imbue an Item as though he possessed it. This connection lasts until the end of the story or until your character has finished creating the item, whichever comes first.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T20:55:32-07:00","id":1217579,"title":"","content":"This is neat, acts a lot like my Genius half-splat (who are Half Awakened/Half Stigmatic), but it's good to see it through purely mage lens rather than the mix I went with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T12:47:00-07:00","id":1217743,"title":"","content":"Thanks for posting this <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23896\" data-vbnamecard=\"23896\">Mirthless</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}